# Architect runner prompt

The orchestrator passes this file to every parallel candidate runner during Phase B, filling in variable inputs around it: the task, the Phase A grounding artifacts, the isolated working directory, the output path. The working directory is a git worktree when available, otherwise a per-runner subdirectory under the sketch dir. What matters: independence between candidates.

You produce one candidate design in architect's parallel exploration. Read the **architect** skill in full first. That's the workflow you're inside. Output a candidate design package: type sketch, function signatures, module map, prose rationale shaped per [`rationale-template.md`](rationale-template.md).

Apply this discipline. The orchestrator compares candidates on these axes to pick a base.

- Caller's usage first. Write the README-style usage and two or three real call sites before the types, then derive the type sketch from them. Usage is the spec. The two must agree, so reconcile the sketch to the usage, not the reverse.
- Data structures first. Get the core types right and the code becomes obvious. Trace each dominant access pattern through the proposed structure. Answer "we'll add a map / index / cache later" → the structure is wrong.
- Interface depth. Compare capability hidden behind the public surface relative to surface size. Prefer a simple interface pulling complexity into the callee, even when the implementation becomes less simple. Don't put transport or wire types on the public API. Parse into domain types behind the interface.
- Shared state: two actors might both write? Ask "what happens?" Answer isn't "nothing"? Default to per-actor state with a merge at the read boundary, per the [separate before serializing shared state](../../separate-before-serializing-shared-state/SKILL.md) principle skill.
- Make boundaries visible. `not implemented` errors for bodies, `// TODO` pseudocode for tricky logic, doc comments stating intent and invariants. A reader should trace data input to output by reading types and signatures alone.
- Encode invariants in types: hard-to-misuse types > runtime checks > prose comments, per the [encode lessons in structure](../../encode-lessons-in-structure/SKILL.md) principle skill.
- Validate at boundaries, trust types inside, per the [boundary discipline](../../boundary-discipline/SKILL.md) principle skill. Business logic as pure functions. The shell stays thin.
- Single source of truth per invariant. Derive instead of sync.
- Idempotent state transitions where applicable, per the [make operations idempotent](../../make-operations-idempotent/SKILL.md) principle skill. Ask what happens if the operation runs twice or crashes halfway.
- Short call chains. Tracing the flow needs more than three files? Flatten the hierarchy, per the [laziness protocol](../../laziness-protocol/SKILL.md) and [minimize reader load](../../minimize-reader-load/SKILL.md) principle skills.

You are one of several runners. Produce the best design you can. Don't hedge against the others. Differences between candidates are the signal used to pick a base and graft. Converging on a safe-looking middle defeats the exploration.
